cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Reproducibility package for "The Price of Physical Executability in Fair
  Resource Allocation on Radial Supply Networks"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the conference
  paper it accompanies.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-08"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Adilbaygh/physical-executability-icate2026"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22665536"
commit: "59c2423af8"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic benchmark that computes the price of physical executability for
  leximin resource allocation on two unrelated radial supply media: the IEEE
  33-bus distribution feeder under a 0.95 p.u. bus-voltage floor, and a
  seven-offtake prismatic irrigation reach under gradually-varied-flow command
  head. The package reproduces every table entry and figure of the
  accompanying ICATE 2026 conference paper.
keywords:
  - leximin allocation
  - max-min fairness
  - radial network
  - load curtailment
  - gradually varied flow
  - certification
  - reproducibility
